thought he was an honest citizen,

260
00:10:04,218 --> 00:10:05,500
and you fellas were breaking the law.

261
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:08,019
- [Frank] Apparently sarcasm
hasn't hit the old west yet.

262
00:10:08,019 --> 00:10:09,986
- I guess he must be over the hill by now,

263
00:10:09,986 --> 00:10:13,753
no use chasing him, might as
well call the whole thing off.

264
00:10:13,753 --> 00:10:14,586
- [Clay] To-mah-to!

265
00:10:14,586 --> 00:10:16,003
- [Frank] Tomato!

266
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:21,000
(imitates steady beep)

267
00:10:22,216 --> 00:10:23,422
(chuckles)

268
00:10:23,422 --> 00:10:24,442
I still got it.

269
00:10:24,442 --> 00:10:25,897
(chuckles)

270
00:10:25,897 --> 00:10:28,983
(imitates car engine revs)

271
00:10:28,983 --> 00:10:31,556
(gun shot fires)

272
00:10:31,556 --> 00:10:34,092
- [Clay] Oh God, that stang!

273
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:38,214
- [Frank] Way to go Ted, now
we have to talk to him again.

274
00:10:38,214 --> 00:10:41,301
- [Clay] Please sir, can
we have our bullets back?

275
00:10:41,301 --> 00:10:42,633
- There oughta be a law against the man

276
00:10:42,633 --> 00:10:44,358
who carries and can steal weapons.

277
00:10:44,358 --> 00:10:46,111
You boys get tempted too easy.

278
00:10:46,111 --> 00:10:46,944
Get down.

279
00:10:48,102 --> 00:10:49,807
- [Frank] This is very
awkward 'cause all the horses

280
00:10:49,807 --> 00:10:51,134
are really good friends.

281
00:10:51,134 --> 00:10:53,336
- [Clay] It's pretty embarrassing.

282
00:10:53,336 --> 00:10:55,097
Now line dance!

283
00:10:55,097 --> 00:10:56,399
- Take 'em off or I'll burn 'em off.

284
00:10:56,399 --> 00:10:58,060
- [Frank] Now ask 'em if you can

285
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:00,296
show 'em something in a new buck pump.

286
00:11:00,296 --> 00:11:02,639
- [Clay] Let me help you here Gary,

287
00:11:02,639 --> 00:11:05,515
you had those hammer toes.

288
00:11:05,515 --> 00:11:08,848
- [Frank] Foot fetishes of the old west.

289
00:11:10,424 --> 00:11:11,937
- [Clay] Now say you're
going to check in back

290
00:11:11,937 --> 00:11:13,312
for a size five.

291
00:11:13,312 --> 00:11:14,229
- Drop 'em.

292
00:11:16,023 --> 00:11:17,509
- [Frank] Did I say throw them?

293
00:11:17,509 --> 00:11:18,842
Now do it again.

294
00:11:21,521 --> 00:11:23,529
- [Clay] They're all wearing white clogs.

295
00:11:23,529 --> 00:11:25,546
(playful orchestral music)

296
00:11:25,546 --> 00:11:26,793
(chuckles)

297
00:11:26,793 --> 00:11:29,061
- [Clay] Hey, you've got flat toes.

298
00:11:29,061 --> 00:11:30,838
- [Frank] I miss my spur noises.

299
00:11:30,838 --> 00:11:34,425
- [Clay] Jacksonville,
where church, family,

300
00:11:34,425 --> 00:11:37,195
and hopefully someday
industry, come together,

301
00:11:37,195 --> 00:11:39,862
great big backs of the old west.

302
00:11:42,646 --> 00:11:46,146
- [Frank] Oh no, he just hit a pedestrian.

303
00:11:47,405 --> 00:11:51,405
- [Clay] I'm so sick of
gingham, I could scream.

304
00:11:52,325 --> 00:11:53,169
(chuckles)

305
00:11:53,169 --> 00:11:54,375
I love my job.

306
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:55,452
- How was the trip.

307
00:11:55,452 --> 00:11:57,198
- We were almost held
up over near the pass.

308
00:11:57,198 --> 00:11:58,615
- Yeah? What do you mean almost?

309
00:11:58,615 --> 00:12:00,013
- I'm carrying a big shipment,

310
00:12:00,013 --> 00:12:01,707
I wasn't taking any chances.

311
00:12:01,707 --> 00:12:03,501
I was watching the road
ahead about half a mile

312
00:12:03,501 --> 00:12:05,342
and I seen this mass parts,

313
00:12:05,342 --> 00:12:07,617
by the time we got around
the bend, he was gone.

314
00:12:07,617 --> 00:12:09,213
- All right, we'll try and round him up.

315
00:12:09,213 --> 00:12:10,563
Get the horses Chuck.

316
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:11,773
What'd he look like Tom?

317
00:12:11,773 --> 00:12:13,794
- Oh he was a big fella, his own horse,

318
00:12:13,794 --> 00:12:15,003
had a black bandana.

319
00:12:15,003 --> 00:12:16,326
- [Frank] Beautiful thighs.

320
00:12:16,326 --> 00:12:18,020
- That's good enough for me, see ya later.

321
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:19,222
- [Frank] Nice tummy.

322
00:12:19,222 --> 00:12:20,683
- Go help Mrs. Bigsby and Mrs. Jones.

323
00:12:20,683 --> 00:12:22,280
Now look, everything
is gonna be all right,

324
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:24,266
break it up folks, break it up.

325
00:12:24,266 --> 00:12:28,317
- [Clay] Go on home and
disappoint your husbands.

326
00:12:28,317 --> 00:12:30,288
- [Frank] Ew, look at the all poo.

327
00:12:30,288 --> 00:12:31,972
(groans in disgust)

328
00:12:31,972 --> 00:12:33,870
Whoop, one of my tires is low.

329
00:12:33,870 --> 00:12:37,203
(slow orchestral music)

330
00:12:38,065 --> 00:12:41,849
(air bursts jokingly)

331
00:12:41,849 --> 00:12:44,580
I will not let you not buy this shoe.

332
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:46,036
(chuckles)

333
00:12:46,036 --> 00:12:49,514
- [Clay] I couldn't help, that tickles.

334
00:12:49,514 --> 00:12:52,681
- [Frank] I wasn't playing shoe store!

335
00:12:53,809 --> 00:12:55,075
- [Clay] You know, his horse has the look

336
00:12:55,075 --> 00:12:59,242
of someone who spent a lot
of time humoring his master.

337
00:13:00,078 --> 00:13:01,092
- [Cowboy] Hello there!

338
00:13:01,092 --> 00:13:01,981
- [Frank] Hello there!

339
00:13:01,981 --> 00:13:03,736
- I just had a little trouble.

340
00:13:03,736 --> 00:13:05,581
My horse threw a shoe.

341
00:13:05,581 --> 00:13:06,612
- [Clay] Ate a ringer.

342
00:13:06,612 --> 00:13:07,761
- Oh that's too bad.

343
00:13:07,761 --> 00:13:09,188
I think you can get him
reshot up at the ranch.

344
00:13:09,188 --> 00:13:11,102
- Which ranch?

345
00:13:11,102 --> 00:13:12,538
- Double C.

346
00:13:12,538 --> 00:13:14,704
- Oh that's fine. Where is it?

347
00:13:14,704 --> 00:13:15,828
- [Frank] What an idiot.

348
00:13:15,828 --> 00:13:18,845
- You're on it, covers
practically the entire valley.

349
00:13:18,845 --> 00:13:19,958
- [Frank] And most of the world!

350
00:13:19,958 --> 00:13:22,143
- The ranch house is up over
the next hill about a mile.

351
00:13:22,143 --> 00:13:22,976
- Thanks.

352
00:13:24,187 --> 00:13:26,194
Say, it's lucky for me you happened along,

353
00:13:26,194 --> 00:13:29,054
otherwise I mighta had to walk.

354
00:13:29,054 --> 00:13:33,208
- I got news for you,
you're still gonna walk.

355
00:13:33,208 --> 00:13:35,125
- [Clay] Yippe-yi-ouch!

356
00:13:37,056 --> 00:13:38,473
Oh good one boss!

357
00:13:40,018 --> 00:13:42,381
Maybe I could just hold
on to your horse's tail

358
00:13:42,381 --> 00:13:44,759
and you could drag me
or something, I dunno.

359
00:13:44,759 --> 00:13:49,301
- [Frank] The Double
Cranch? What is that about?

360
00:13:49,301 --> 00:13:52,634
It's a sprawling studio apartment ranch.

361
00:13:53,926 --> 00:13:57,920
- Who's Jane bringing home with her now?

362
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,490
- [Frank] How do you like this one dad?

363
00:13:59,490 --> 00:14:00,323
- Hello dad.

364
00:14:00,323 --> 00:14:01,398
- [Dad] Hello dear.

365
00:14:01,398 --> 00:14:03,391
- [Frank] Hello dear.

366
00:14:03,391 --> 00:14:05,047
- Why sure he can have
a shoe for his horse,

367
00:14:05,047 --> 00:14:06,964
we got more shoes than we have horses.

368
00:14:06,964 --> 00:14:08,196
- [Clay] Dad's mental.

369
00:14:08,196 --> 00:14:10,564
- Four legs to one horse, hey Slim,

370
00:14:10,564 --> 00:14:12,589
go and shoe this fella's horse.

371
00:14:12,589 --> 00:14:13,422
- Thanks.

372
00:14:15,774 --> 00:14:19,409
- You look like you could
stand something cool and wet.

373
00:14:19,409 --> 00:14:20,455
- [Clay] Dad!

374
00:14:20,455 --> 00:14:22,947
- I sure could, so could my feet.

375
00:14:22,947 --> 00:14:24,913
- [Frank] Get his feet
a glass of lemonade.

376
00:14:24,913 --> 00:14:27,397
- Well don't just stand
there, go get us a drink.

377
00:14:27,397 --> 00:14:28,844
- Yes dad.

378
00:14:28,844 --> 00:14:30,473
- Get on this Remy.

379
00:14:30,473 --> 00:14:31,978
♫ Dah da da da da

380
00:14:31,978 --> 00:14:34,200
♫ Dah da da da da dah ♫

381
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,568
- I like the property you got around here.

382
00:14:35,568 --> 00:14:36,862
- [Clay] Real dysfunctional.

383
00:14:36,862 --> 00:14:38,301
- Yeah built it all up myself,

384
00:14:38,301 --> 00:14:40,661
started from scratch with
a brood of wild mares.

385
00:14:40,661 --> 00:14:44,664
Never would stop expanding
if it hadn't been for this.

386
00:14:44,664 --> 00:14:46,543
- [Frank] Oh well now I'm expanding, ha!

387
00:14:46,543 --> 00:14:47,804
- I got in a stampede one night

388
00:14:47,804 --> 00:14:49,525
and bust myself up good.

389
00:14:49,525 --> 00:14:50,924
Ever since then, I turned over most

390
00:14:50,924 --> 00:14:52,644
of the management to Riley.

391
00:14:52,644 --> 00:14:54,708
- [Clay] Oh that's nice,
where's your daughter?

392
00:14:54,708 --> 00:14:56,387
- Must be a lot of wild
horses in this part

393
00:14:56,387 --> 00:14:57,421
of the country.

394
00:14:57,421 --> 00:15:00,226
- No, no (mumbles).

395
00:15:00,226 --> 00:15:01,989
- [Frank] His doppleganger.

396
00:15:01,989 --> 00:15:03,652
- Couple?

397
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:05,471
- From the small ranch owners,

398
00:15:05,471 --> 00:15:06,744
they claim that we're the cause of it,

399
00:15:06,744 --> 00:15:08,532
that we're taking too
many mares from the herd.

400
00:15:08,532 --> 00:15:10,026
- Ah let them claim whatever they want.

401
00:15:10,026 --> 00:15:11,610
- [Clay] Tourette's of the old west.

402
00:15:11,610 --> 00:15:14,249
- They don't like it, they know that...

403
00:15:14,249 --> 00:15:15,634
- Looks like you're the one

404
00:15:15,634 --> 00:15:17,306
who could use something cool now.

405
00:15:17,306 --> 00:15:21,473
- [Frank] Hi I'm Susan,
I'll be your daughter today.

406
00:15:22,417 --> 00:15:25,000
- [Clay] Oh quit giving me pee.

407
00:15:27,563 --> 00:15:30,480
(upbeat pop music)

408
00:15:33,716 --> 00:15:35,341
(playful orchestral music)

409
00:15:35,341 --> 00:15:37,650
- [Clay] Curly and anti-Curly.

410
00:15:37,650 --> 00:15:41,025
- Afternoon Miss Jane, Mr. Cooper, Riley.

411
00:15:41,025 --> 00:15:42,889
- Well sheriff, what brings you here?

412
00:15:42,889 --> 00:15:45,156
- Oh I'm trying to pick
up a fella's trail.

413
00:15:45,156 --> 00:15:47,678
(mumbles) just pulled into Jacksonville

414
00:15:47,678 --> 00:15:50,555
a little while ago and
reported seeing a mountain man

415
00:15:50,555 --> 00:15:52,827
down to the big gun (mumbles).

416
00:15:52,827 --> 00:15:54,122
- Sit down sheriff.

417
00:15:54,122 --> 00:15:55,210
- Thanks Jane.

418
00:15:55,210 --> 00:15:56,503
- [Frank] That's a long sentence

419
00:15:56,503 --> 00:15:57,619
and you're probably tired.

420
00:15:57,619 --> 00:15:58,882
- Howdy.

421
00:15:58,882 --> 00:16:01,122
(mumbles)

422
00:16:01,122 --> 00:16:03,603
- No, we had a couple extra guys

423
00:16:03,603 --> 00:16:05,279
planting the coast.

424
00:16:05,279 --> 00:16:07,440
The guy riding on the seat
was watching the road ahead

425
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:09,857
for about a half a mile
through field glasses.

426
00:16:09,857 --> 00:16:10,956
- [Clay] Fascinating.

427
00:16:10,956 --> 00:16:12,522
- By the time they got to the pass,

428
00:16:12,522 --> 00:16:13,852
the masked men had gone.

429
00:16:13,852 --> 00:16:14,685
- [Clay] It's me.

430
00:16:14,685 --> 00:16:16,164
(coughs) It's me.

431
00:16:16,164 --> 00:16:17,638
- I sure woulda liked to seen the look

432
00:16:17,638 --> 00:16:19,479
on that fella's face if he'd have tried

433
00:16:19,479 --> 00:16:21,038
to stick up that stage.

434
00:16:21,038 --> 00:16:22,070
(chuckles)

435
00:16:22,070 --> 00:16:23,542
- [Frank] The joke is on the sheriff.

436
00:16:23,542 --> 00:16:26,578
(chuckles)

437
00:16:26,578 --> 00:16:28,726
- Did the guard get a good look at him?

438
00:16:28,726 --> 00:16:32,066
- Yeah as good as you could
from a half a mile away

439
00:16:32,066 --> 00:16:34,515
through field glasses.

440
00:16:34,515 --> 00:16:38,030
Said he was big, was wearing
a black bandana for a mask,

441
00:16:38,030 --> 00:16:40,303
and riding the wrong horse.

442
00:16:40,303 --> 00:16:42,184
- [Clay] Well actually,
my scarf is dark navy

443
00:16:42,184 --> 00:16:43,294
and so is my horse.

444
00:16:43,294 --> 00:16:45,254
- I (mumbles) your job sheriff,

445
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:46,890
this country must be full of big fellas

446
00:16:46,890 --> 00:16:49,534
wearing black bandanas
and riding around horses.

447
00:16:49,534 --> 00:16:51,124
- [Frank] Everyone here is so fun!

448
00:16:51,124 --> 00:16:52,624
- No, not so many.

449
00:16:54,223 --> 00:16:57,408
- [Clay] Say, you got a
sweet outlaw ass, don't you?

450
00:16:57,408 --> 00:16:58,491
- You're big.

451
00:16:59,676 --> 00:17:03,221
Unless I'm mistaken, that's a
black bandana you're wearing.

452
00:17:03,221 --> 00:17:05,443
- [Frank] They are falling
for each other hard.

453
00:17:05,443 --> 00:17:08,265
- What kind of horse was
this man riding Mr. Cooper?

454
00:17:08,265 --> 00:17:10,196
- [Frank] It was just a head and a stick,

455
00:17:10,196 --> 00:17:11,269
it was weird!

456
00:17:11,269 --> 00:17:12,102
- A roan.

457
00:17:12,966 --> 00:17:14,963
- [Frank] I could explain,
it was a loaner roan.

458
00:17:14,963 --> 00:17:16,699
- Something wrong sheriff?

459
00:17:16,699 --> 00:17:18,426
I wasn't near the pass.

460
00:17:18,426 --> 00:17:20,899
I came up through the valley.

461
00:17:20,899 --> 00:17:24,818
- [Frank] Let's go barefoot all summer.

462
00:17:24,818 --> 00:17:25,850
- [Clay] Yep well that's just me,

463
00:17:25,850 --> 00:17:28,550
I gotta have an art support in a firm.

464
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:30,883
- Come on, give me your gun.

465
00:17:33,004 --> 00:17:34,491
- [Frank] Well, they'll do that sometimes.

466
00:17:34,491 --> 00:17:36,515
- Well I guess my horse
outta be shot by now,

467
00:17:36,515 --> 00:17:37,726
thanks a lot Mr. Cooper.

468
00:17:37,726 --> 00:17:38,828
- Freeze.

469
00:17:38,828 --> 00:17:40,229
- [Frank] Oh, they're playing freeze tag.

470
00:17:40,229 --> 00:17:41,328
- What's this all about Rocky?

471
00:17:41,328 --> 00:17:42,633
- Every shot Hank?

472
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:43,867
He made us get off our horses,

473
00:17:43,867 --> 00:17:45,786
stampede them, and then took our guns.

474
00:17:45,786 --> 00:17:47,099
- Took your boots too I see.

475
00:17:47,099 --> 00:17:49,016
- [Frank] Shut up Iris.

476
00:17:50,809 --> 00:17:52,994
- What have you got to say for yourself?

477
00:17:52,994 --> 00:17:54,733
- Part of what he says is right.

478
00:17:54,733 --> 00:17:58,414
- [Clay] Yeah, them
other part is right too.

479
00:17:58,414 --> 00:18:00,069
- They just thought I'd be laying a little

480
00:18:00,069 --> 00:18:01,968
and give the kid a break,
but he took a shot at me.

481
00:18:01,968 --> 00:18:03,718
- [Clay] I'm so lost.

482
00:18:05,104 --> 00:18:07,096
- I don't like any unnecessary gun play

483
00:18:07,096 --> 00:18:08,786
going on in my jurisdiction.

484
00:18:08,786 --> 00:18:11,304
You're gonna have to answer
to a charge of assault

485
00:18:11,304 --> 00:18:13,504
and that just places you down at the pass,

486
00:18:13,504 --> 00:18:16,013
which is another a little
matter I wanna get cleaned up.

487
00:18:16,013 --> 00:18:17,412
Let's go.

488
00:18:17,412 --> 00:18:18,728
Put it away Rocky.

489
00:18:18,728 --> 00:18:20,098
- [Clay] Yeah and we're gonna
pin the cattle wrestling

490
00:18:20,098 --> 00:18:23,301
from last year on you
too, if you don't mind.

491
00:18:23,301 --> 00:18:24,767
- [Frank] He's wearing chick jeans,

492
00:18:24,767 --> 00:18:26,100
they fit better!

493
00:18:27,123 --> 00:18:29,325
He drank our apple juice.

494
00:18:29,325 --> 00:18:31,491
- (mumbles) close enough to tell for sure.

495
00:18:31,491 --> 00:18:34,473
- I suppose you took a
couple of pot shots at them?

496
00:18:34,473 --> 00:18:36,851
- Well yes, but we were
only trying to scare him--

497
00:18:36,851 --> 00:18:38,840
- Haven't we got enough
trouble in this valley

498
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:40,639
without my men making more?

499
00:18:40,639 --> 00:18:41,472
- [Frank] No.

500
00:18:41,472 --> 00:18:42,382
- Riley, get him out of my sight

501
00:18:42,382 --> 00:18:43,915
before I have him thrown off the ranch.

502
00:18:43,915 --> 00:18:46,940
I warned you before Rocky
about being trigger happy.

503
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:48,923
- I wanna talk to you.

504
00:18:48,923 --> 00:18:51,020
- [Clay] Glad we had this
little face to groin talk.

505
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:53,502
- I told you to be careful
whenever you made a move,

506
00:18:53,502 --> 00:18:54,923
next time you go after anyone,

507
00:18:54,923 --> 00:18:56,841
be sure there are no witnesses around.

508
00:18:56,841 --> 00:18:58,245
- This fella came out of nowhere.

509
00:18:58,245 --> 00:19:00,252
- Well watch your step from now on.

510
00:19:00,252 --> 00:19:02,365
Things are going too good to spoil.

511
00:19:02,365 --> 00:19:04,547
I got the old man so he won't budge.

512
00:19:04,547 --> 00:19:05,899
- [Clay] I put a rock behind his wheel.

513
00:19:05,899 --> 00:19:07,402
- I want you to push the
small ranchers around

514
00:19:07,402 --> 00:19:08,991
until they won't take anymore,

515
