00:44:21,994 --> 00:44:25,827
- [Tom Sirvo] Oh hop
sing is making chow mein.

1264
00:44:27,638 --> 00:44:31,186
- [Croooow] This is a
gripping Levi's commercial.

1265
00:44:31,186 --> 00:44:32,218
♫ Hi ho

1266
00:44:32,218 --> 00:44:33,267
♫ Hi ho

1267
00:44:33,267 --> 00:44:35,251
♫ It's off to work we go ♫

1268
00:44:35,251 --> 00:44:37,648
(door knocks)

1269
00:44:37,648 --> 00:44:39,092
- [Croooow] We've come a courting,

1270
00:44:39,092 --> 00:44:40,852
delivering their funds a popping.

1271
00:44:40,852 --> 00:44:42,043
- Hello Mr. Ferguson.

1272
00:44:42,043 --> 00:44:43,363
- We'd like to see your father Jane.

1273
00:44:43,363 --> 00:44:44,863
- [Mr. Cooper] Jane? Who is it?

1274
00:44:44,863 --> 00:44:46,130
- Ferguson dad.

1275
00:44:46,130 --> 00:44:47,065
- Oh hello Pete.

1276
00:44:47,065 --> 00:44:47,941
- [Croooow] Ow!

1277
00:44:47,941 --> 00:44:48,882
- Hi boys.

1278
00:44:48,882 --> 00:44:50,213
- [Croooow] Old man, your picante sauce

1279
00:44:50,213 --> 00:44:51,684
is made in New York City!

1280
00:44:51,684 --> 00:44:54,851
- I guess so, it's got Double C on it.

1281
00:44:55,952 --> 00:44:57,943
- It was found down in the meadow.

1282
00:44:57,943 --> 00:45:00,326
- I guess one of the boys, careless.

1283
00:45:00,326 --> 00:45:01,734
- Very careless.

1284
00:45:01,734 --> 00:45:03,729
- [Tom Sirvo] Wow, that's
like a whole foot of ear.

1285
00:45:03,729 --> 00:45:05,060
- What are you driving at?

1286
00:45:05,060 --> 00:45:06,512
- That iron was found down in the meadow

1287
00:45:06,512 --> 00:45:09,267
after some riders drove a
band of wild horses through.

1288
00:45:09,267 --> 00:45:10,647
- [Tom Sirvo] This is about me, isn't it?

1289
00:45:10,647 --> 00:45:11,846
- Well you're not insinuating

1290
00:45:11,846 --> 00:45:13,188
we've been raiding the herd?

1291
00:45:13,188 --> 00:45:15,230
- We're not insinuating anything Charlie,

1292
00:45:15,230 --> 00:45:16,706
we're just taking tabs.

1293
00:45:16,706 --> 00:45:18,731
- That branding iron might
have been lost a week ago,

1294
00:45:18,731 --> 00:45:20,272
a month ago, anytime.

1295
00:45:20,272 --> 00:45:21,572
- [Voiceover] Well that's possible.

1296
00:45:21,572 --> 00:45:22,756
In that case, you won't object

1297
00:45:22,756 --> 00:45:23,719
to our looking over your stock.

1298
00:45:23,719 --> 00:45:24,798
- You're darn right I object.

1299
00:45:24,798 --> 00:45:25,905
- Oh but now--

1300
00:45:25,905 --> 00:45:27,112
- I'm done with this.

1301
00:45:27,112 --> 00:45:28,440
- [Croooow] Sorry for lending my support.

1302
00:45:28,440 --> 00:45:29,914
- I told you the Double
C hasn't been raiding

1303
00:45:29,914 --> 00:45:30,977
the wild horses.

1304
00:45:30,977 --> 00:45:32,931
I don't propose I have
anybody inspect my stock

1305
00:45:32,931 --> 00:45:34,374
to check up on my word.

1306
00:45:34,374 --> 00:45:36,332
The whole thing's beginning
to look like a frame up.

1307
00:45:36,332 --> 00:45:37,931
I wouldn't be surprised
if one of you fellas

1308
00:45:37,931 --> 00:45:39,042
on the back of the whole thing

1309
00:45:39,042 --> 00:45:40,149
in order to break up the agreement,

1310
00:45:40,149 --> 00:45:41,244
'cause that's the way you want it,

1311
00:45:41,244 --> 00:45:42,284
that's all right with me.

1312
00:45:42,284 --> 00:45:43,642
- Well you said a thing
for silver Mr. Cooper.

1313
00:45:43,642 --> 00:45:44,849
(mumbles)

1314
00:45:44,849 --> 00:45:45,874
(Tom Sirvo grumbles)

1315
00:45:45,874 --> 00:45:47,122
- I'm giving orders, any trespassers

1316
00:45:47,122 --> 00:45:48,976
in the Double C will be shot on sight.

1317
00:45:48,976 --> 00:45:50,512
- [Duke] Mr. Cooper,
you're only buying yourself

1318
00:45:50,512 --> 00:45:51,566
a lot of trouble.

1319
00:45:51,566 --> 00:45:52,729
- I can pay for anything I buy.

1320
00:45:52,729 --> 00:45:55,563
- [Croooow] Nah, nah, nah, nah, nah.

1321
00:45:55,563 --> 00:45:59,586
- [Tom Sirvo] Kindergarten
baby, wash your face in gravy,

1322
00:45:59,586 --> 00:46:03,505
wrap it up in bubblegum, and
send it to the navy, nah.

1323
00:46:03,505 --> 00:46:04,527
- [Croooow] Hey come on, I was kidding!

1324
00:46:04,527 --> 00:46:05,696
Hey wait!

1325
00:46:05,696 --> 00:46:07,327
And they still had to pay parking,

1326
00:46:07,327 --> 00:46:09,456
the Double Cranch does not validate.

1327
00:46:09,456 --> 00:46:12,510
- I don't think you
realize what this means.

1328
00:46:12,510 --> 00:46:14,535
- Well they've left me no other choice.

1329
00:46:14,535 --> 00:46:15,368
- Look dad--

1330
00:46:15,368 --> 00:46:16,361
- No please Jane.

1331
00:46:16,361 --> 00:46:18,212
- [Croooow] Get the doomsday machine.

1332
00:46:18,212 --> 00:46:21,739
(ominous orchestral music)

1333
00:46:21,739 --> 00:46:22,572
- Riley!

1334
00:46:22,572 --> 00:46:23,571
- [Tom Sirvo] I wasn't listening!

1335
00:46:23,571 --> 00:46:25,419
- [Croooow] He's the George
Stefanopolis of the ranch.

1336
00:46:25,419 --> 00:46:26,641
- [Tom Sirvo] Snuffleofogus.

1337
00:46:26,641 --> 00:46:27,745
George Snuffleofogus.

1338
00:46:27,745 --> 00:46:29,307
- I just told Pete Ferguson and the boys

1339
00:46:29,307 --> 00:46:31,040
if there's any trespassers
on the Double C,

1340
00:46:31,040 --> 00:46:32,007
they'll be shot.

1341
00:46:32,007 --> 00:46:33,592
- [Croooow] Send out a press
release to that effect.

1342
00:46:33,592 --> 00:46:34,864
- Why not let the sheriff handle it?

1343
00:46:34,864 --> 00:46:35,999
- Those are orders Riley.

1344
00:46:35,999 --> 00:46:36,993
- Don't you see?

1345
00:46:36,993 --> 00:46:38,110
Then if they come on your ranch,

1346
00:46:38,110 --> 00:46:39,302
you'll have the law on your side,

1347
00:46:39,302 --> 00:46:40,932
you'll be entitled to protection.

1348
00:46:40,932 --> 00:46:43,351
- [Tom Sirvo] Oh once again,
I'm putty in your hands.

1349
00:46:43,351 --> 00:46:45,050
I'll go over here.

1350
00:46:45,050 --> 00:46:47,897
- I guess I lost my head.

1351
00:46:47,897 --> 00:46:50,887
Maybe that's the best way to handle it.

1352
00:46:50,887 --> 00:46:52,276
(mumbles)

1353
00:46:52,276 --> 00:46:56,054
- [Tom Sirvo] John Waters, Texas ranger.

1354
00:46:56,054 --> 00:46:57,686
- For a while last night, it looked as if

1355
00:46:57,686 --> 00:46:59,688
the whole thing was bust wide open.

1356
00:46:59,688 --> 00:47:01,622
- You know, I had a feeling
it wasn't gonna last.

1357
00:47:01,622 --> 00:47:03,399
- [Croooow] It was a great brunch though.

1358
00:47:03,399 --> 00:47:04,482
- Protection.

1359
00:47:07,909 --> 00:47:10,643
I can round up some men and swear 'em in.

1360
00:47:10,643 --> 00:47:12,810
- You won't have to look for any deputies.

1361
00:47:12,810 --> 00:47:14,687
- [Tom Sirvo] I hear
my rotisserie baseball.

1362
00:47:14,687 --> 00:47:18,193
- [Croooow] Let's see,
dear sheriff I like you,

1363
00:47:18,193 --> 00:47:19,340
do you like me?

1364
00:47:19,340 --> 00:47:20,759
Check one.

1365
00:47:20,759 --> 00:47:23,106
- These are Double C men.

1366
00:47:23,106 --> 00:47:24,650
- [Tom Sirvo] Double Semen!

1367
00:47:24,650 --> 00:47:25,609
(chuckles)

1368
00:47:25,609 --> 00:47:26,813
- [Croooow] Don't touch me.

1369
00:47:26,813 --> 00:47:28,759
- We're picking our own deputies.

1370
00:47:28,759 --> 00:47:30,759
- Not while I'm sheriff.

1371
00:47:32,366 --> 00:47:33,621
- [Tom Sirvo] Wait, I'll be right up there

1372
00:47:33,621 --> 00:47:35,305
and then I'll retort.

1373
00:47:35,305 --> 00:47:37,421
- Maybe we can do
something about that too.

1374
00:47:37,421 --> 00:47:39,091
- [Croooow] I'd love to bite
the bridge of your nose.

1375
00:47:39,091 --> 00:47:41,078
- Are you forgetting that
Cooper put you in this job?

1376
00:47:41,078 --> 00:47:44,016
- [Tom Sirvo] El
Demando's of the old west.

1377
00:47:44,016 --> 00:47:45,849
- Well what's it gonna be?

1378
00:47:45,849 --> 00:47:47,932
Our deputies or your job?

1379
00:47:50,799 --> 00:47:53,057
- [Croooow] So, is that
the end of the scene

1380
00:47:53,057 --> 00:47:54,281
or do you have another...

1381
00:47:54,281 --> 00:47:55,682
No that's it, okay.

1382
00:47:55,682 --> 00:47:57,269
- [Riley] Now remember, you're deputites.

1383
00:47:57,269 --> 00:47:58,621
- [Tom Sirvo] Why thank you.

1384
00:47:58,621 --> 00:48:01,239
- No matter what you do,
you got the law on your side

1385
00:48:01,239 --> 00:48:03,537
and if someone should
accidentally be killed

1386
00:48:03,537 --> 00:48:07,584
while resisting arrest, that's too bad.

1387
00:48:07,584 --> 00:48:09,560
- [Tom Sirvo] Huh, huh? Get it?

1388
00:48:09,560 --> 00:48:10,851
Kill guys!

1389
00:48:10,851 --> 00:48:12,429
- [Croooow] Can we do anything sir?

1390
00:48:12,429 --> 00:48:13,543
Can we burn puppies?

1391
00:48:13,543 --> 00:48:14,654
- Maybe this will come in handy

1392
00:48:14,654 --> 00:48:16,284
to settle some personal affairs.

1393
00:48:16,284 --> 00:48:18,092
- [Croooow] Now there's a man
who understands me, thank you.

1394
00:48:18,092 --> 00:48:22,259
- [Tom Sirvo] Now go do that
voodoo that you do so well.

1395
00:48:24,038 --> 00:48:25,547
- [Croooow] We got the law on our side,

1396
00:48:25,547 --> 00:48:26,896
I'm gonna fail to yield!

1397
00:48:26,896 --> 00:48:28,119
Woo!

1398
00:48:28,119 --> 00:48:29,611
- [Tom Sirvo] Give it up for my posse!

1399
00:48:29,611 --> 00:48:30,871
Woo!

1400
00:48:30,871 --> 00:48:32,702
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1401
00:48:32,702 --> 00:48:34,611
- [Croooow] Uh guys, it's not as much fun

1402
00:48:34,611 --> 00:48:36,175
as I thought it would be.

1403
00:48:36,175 --> 00:48:40,340
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1404
00:48:40,340 --> 00:48:43,055
- [Tom Sirvo] Hey don't push, I'm going.

1405
00:48:43,055 --> 00:48:44,382
(drums whimsically)

1406
00:48:44,382 --> 00:48:46,269
Now fly my horsies, fly!

1407
00:48:46,269 --> 00:48:47,526
(cackles evilly)

1408
00:48:47,526 --> 00:48:48,504
- [Croooow] I'm not leaving!

1409
00:48:48,504 --> 00:48:49,482
Just because the rest of you are doing it,

1410
00:48:49,482 --> 00:48:50,815
I don't have to.

1411
00:48:52,675 --> 00:48:56,085
Let's all go to Fort Lauderdale.

1412
00:48:56,085 --> 00:48:58,585
- [Tom Sirvo] Oh, blew a tire.

1413
00:48:59,940 --> 00:49:01,180
- [Croooow] I don't
think you're supposed to

1414
00:49:01,180 --> 00:49:03,097
burn your own barn Ted.

1415
00:49:04,055 --> 00:49:06,715
Well, quick cup of Joe, then back at it.

1416
00:49:06,715 --> 00:49:07,834
(imitates fart)

1417
00:49:07,834 --> 00:49:09,500
(chuckles)

1418
00:49:09,500 --> 00:49:10,712
- [Tom Sirvo] Funny!

1419
00:49:10,712 --> 00:49:11,970
- What do you want here?

1420
00:49:11,970 --> 00:49:13,108
- Just checking your horses to see

1421
00:49:13,108 --> 00:49:15,470
if there's any Double C
brands in your corral.

1422
00:49:15,470 --> 00:49:17,543
- Get off my place,
there's no Double C horses

1423
00:49:17,543 --> 00:49:18,711
in my corral.

1424
00:49:18,711 --> 00:49:20,032
- [Tom Sirvo] Then if you wouldn't mind

1425
00:49:20,032 --> 00:49:21,358
doing me the service of dying!

1426
00:49:21,358 --> 00:49:22,726
(gun shots blast)

1427
00:49:22,726 --> 00:49:24,484
- You're getting Double C horses now.

1428
00:49:24,484 --> 00:49:26,029
- [Croooow] If you were alive, you'd hear

1429
00:49:26,029 --> 00:49:27,612
that ironic retort.

1430
00:49:28,659 --> 00:49:31,108
The ton ton macoots of the old west!

1431
00:49:31,108 --> 00:49:33,062
- [Tom Sirvo] Old timer Billy Slater, no!

1432
00:49:33,062 --> 00:49:35,559
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1433
00:49:35,559 --> 00:49:37,810
- [Croooow] No, I don't
wanna live with grandma!

1434
00:49:37,810 --> 00:49:40,120
- [Tom Sirvo] This guy
wouldn't even be a greeter

1435
00:49:40,120 --> 00:49:41,925
at Roy Rogers.

1436
00:49:41,925 --> 00:49:45,149
- [Croooow] Hey, he transmigerfied.

1437
00:49:45,149 --> 00:49:46,712
He's thinner.

1438
00:49:46,712 --> 00:49:49,870
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1439
00:49:49,870 --> 00:49:52,473
You never liked him, neighbor declares.

1440
00:49:52,473 --> 00:49:54,909
- [Tom Sirvo] Building code
invented and under fire.

1441
00:49:54,909 --> 00:49:57,659
At least there's no Art Buckwald.

1442
00:49:59,324 --> 00:50:02,429
(hums whimsically)

1443
00:50:02,429 --> 00:50:04,826
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1444
00:50:04,826 --> 00:50:06,759
- [Croooow] Word exonerated is invented.

1445
00:50:06,759 --> 00:50:10,838
- [Tom Sirvo] Literacy rate rises to 1%.

1446
00:50:10,838 --> 00:50:13,279
- [Mike] Look at that,
the orcs are involved.

1447
00:50:13,279 --> 00:50:17,992
(suspenseful orchestral music)

1448
00:50:17,992 --> 00:50:19,219
- [Croooow] Siamese horses.

1449
00:50:19,219 --> 00:50:20,412
- [Tom Sirvo] Dan Roan and Dick Martin

1450
00:50:20,412 --> 00:50:22,382
in Once Upon a Horse.

1451
00:50:22,382 --> 00:50:24,196
- [Mike] It was a great movie.

1452
00:50:24,196 --> 00:50:25,379
Wasn't it once fun?

1453
00:50:25,379 --> 00:50:26,857
- [Tom Sirvo] You guys,
we have the whole prairie,

1454
00:50:26,857 --> 00:50:29,415
do we have to bunch up like this?

1455
00:50:29,415 --> 00:50:33,582
- [Croooow] How many of you
already know about Amway?

1456
00:50:34,955 --> 00:50:36,643
- Remedy like us, were to join us.

1457
00:50:36,643 --> 00:50:37,794
- [Tom Sirvo] Plop, plop.

1458
00:50:37,794 --> 00:50:40,294
(plops erupt)

1459
00:50:43,024 --> 00:50:44,340
Howdy Hitler!

1460
00:50:44,340 --> 00:50:46,084
- I'm asking you to go back to your homes

1461
00:50:46,084 --> 00:50:47,505
and your ranches quietly.

1462
00:50:47,505 --> 00:50:48,338
- [Croooow] But I live in a trailer.

1463
00:50:48,338 --> 00:50:50,648
- Who's gonna answer for Ferguson's death?

1464
00:50:50,648 --> 00:50:52,499
- [Tom Sirvo] What'd he say?

1465
00:50:52,499 --> 00:50:54,804
Louder, can't hear you back here!

1466
00:50:54,804 --> 00:50:56,110
- Catch up with Ferguson's killer,

1467
00:50:56,110 --> 00:50:58,101
let the sheriff handle the Ferguson case,

1468
00:50:58,101 --> 00:51:00,023
pop violence isn't the answer.

1469
00:51:00,023 --> 00:51:01,258
- [Tom Sirvo] Who's
that guy way over there?

1470
00:51:01,258 --> 00:51:02,418
- [Croooow] Shy.

1471
00:51:02,418 --> 00:51:03,783
Flop drop at 10, pass it on.

1472
00:51:03,783 --> 00:51:07,701
- [Voiceover] How do we know
you ain't in Cooper's pay?

1473
00:51:07,701 --> 00:51:09,479
- No I'm not in Cooper's pay--

1474
00:51:09,479 --> 00:51:11,062
- [Tom Sirvo] But don't pick at that.

1475
00:51:11,062 --> 00:51:12,640
- I'm not gonna stand by and
watch a range war break out

1476
00:51:12,640 --> 00:51:14,062
if I can possibly help it.

1477
00:51:14,062 --> 00:51:15,961
- Clem, you're talking like a fool.

1478
00:51:15,961 --> 00:51:17,521
- [Voiceover] Cooper broke his word.

1479
00:51:17,521 --> 00:51:19,562
- [Croooow] Yeah pass
and we won't kill him.

1480
00:51:19,562 --> 00:51:20,701
- [Tom Sirvo] Yeah!

1481
00:51:20,701 --> 00:51:21,942
- He might listen to me.

1482
00:51:21,942 --> 00:51:23,204
He knows I don't own a ranch,

1483
00:51:23,204 --> 00:51:25,082
so I don't have nothing personal to gain.

1484
00:51:25,082 --> 00:51:27,195
At least let me try before you all

1485
00:51:27,195 --> 00:51:29,026
do something you might all regret.

1486
00:51:29,026 --> 00:51:31,295
Go on back to your
ranches, give me a chance

1487
00:51:31,295 --> 00:51:33,338
to talk to Cooper alone.

1488
00:51:33,338 --> 00:51:34,993
- [Croooow] Yeah, I got
it down at flea farm,

1489
00:51:34,993 --> 00:51:36,871
they had real good deal, they
were having a special on us.

1490
00:51:36,871 --> 00:51:38,986
- You know what he's saying is (mumbles).

1491
00:51:38,986 --> 00:51:40,765
Now why don't you all go home.

1492
00:51:40,765 --> 00:51:41,953
- [Tom Sirvo] See where Oklahoma

1493
00:51:41,953 --> 00:51:43,070
wants to be a state?

1494
00:51:43,070 --> 00:51:44,775
Can you believe that?

1495
00:51:44,775 --> 00:51:46,262
- [Mike] Now there are acid burns

1496
00:51:46,262 --> 00:51:48,201
all over this part of the prairie.

1497
00:51:48,201 --> 00:51:50,403
- [Croooow] Wait everybody,
this means we have to go home

1498
00:51:50,403 --> 00:51:51,838
to our wives.

1499
00:51:51,838 --> 00:51:53,139
- [Tom Sirvo] Shit.

1500
00:51:53,139 --> 00:51:56,947
- [Mike] Yeah look at those horse's asses.

1501
00:51:56,947 --> 00:51:58,862
(sweet orchestral music)

1502
00:51:58,862 --> 00:52:00,141
- I got your message.

1503
00:52:00,141 --> 00:52:01,805
- I want to see your father.

1504
00:52:01,805 --> 00:52:05,624
- [Mike] Well I hope you
two will be very happy.

1505
00:52:05,624 --> 00:52:07,044
- I only want to talk to him.

1506
00:52:07,044 --> 00:52:08,040
- [Tom Sirvo] Here's your power drill.

1507
00:52:08,040 --> 00:52:09,069
- I don't think he'll see you.

1508
00:52:09,069 --> 00:52:11,056
- Somebody's gotta make him
realize what's happening.

1509
00:52:11,056 --> 00:52:13,736
The small ranchers are up
in arms over the killing.

1510
00:52:13,736 --> 00:52:15,405
- [Croooow] So this isn't a date?

1511
00:52:15,405 --> 00:52:17,722
- I'd like to help, for your sake.

1512
00:52:17,722 --> 00:52:19,572
- [Mike] Give me time to, no!

1513
00:52:19,572 --> 00:52:21,591
- Thanks (mumbles).

1514
00:52:21,591 --> 00:52:25,817
- [Tom Sirvo] He's the
Lucas Tanner of his time.

1515
00:52:25,817 --> 00:52:27,823
He had this meeting with
a bunch of cowboys today,

1516
00:52:27,823 --> 00:52:29,516
I think it went pretty
well, you shoulda seen me,

1517
00:52:29,516 --> 00:52:31,197
